<title>ESTONIA: TALIBOR AND TALIBID RATES DECREASE SLIGHTLY.</title>
<headline>TALIBOR AND TALIBID RATES DECREASE SLIGHTLY.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central bank of Estonia</p>
<p>said on Wednesday that the Talibor and Talibid interbank loan</p>
<p>averages decreased slightly compared to the previous week.</p>
<p>&quot;A couple of large transactions affected the market,&quot; Erkki</p>
<p>Raasuke, head of Hansapank's interest rate products department</p>
<p>told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Basically the market is waiting for positive news on a</p>
<p>country credit rating and foreign investors are looking for</p>
<p>kroon-denominated assets,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>    TALIBOR/TALIBID    April 2    March 26</p>
<p>    1 week		4.67/3.67   4.77/3.77</p>
<p>    1 month	     6.22/5.22   6.30/5.30</p>
<p>    3 month	     7.98/6.98   8.02/7.02</p>
<p>-- David  Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400</p>
<p>reuters@reuters.ee</p>
